@startuml wowiso pipeline
!theme plain
title wowiso — capture / build / emit pipeline

skinparam rectangle {BackgroundColor #F8FAFC BorderColor #334155}
skinparam package  {BackgroundColor #EEF2FF BorderColor #4F46E5}
skinparam database {BackgroundColor #FEF3C7 BorderColor #B45309}

package "Source box (current Ubuntu)" {
  rectangle "apt-mark showmanual\nsnap list\nflatpak list" as Pkgs
  rectangle "rsync .config /opt .bashrc\n(per-app adapter capture)" as Tree
  rectangle "picker/ Textual tree-picker\n(rules.toml)" as Picker
}

database "manifest.json" as M
database "payload/<profile>/blobs/\n(sha256 deduped)" as Blobs
database "packages.apt / snaps.txt\nflatpaks.txt" as PLists

Pkgs --> PLists --> M
Tree --> Blobs --> M
Picker .. Tree : selects
Picker .. Pkgs : selects

package "build/" {
  rectangle "extract base ISO\n(xorriso -osirrox)" as Extract
  rectangle "inject nocloud seed\nuser-data+meta-data" as Seed
  rectangle "inject payload\n(/wowiso/)" as Pay
  rectangle "edit grub.cfg + isolinux\n(Install/Live/Rescue)" as Menu
  rectangle "(LIVE) mksquashfs" as Sq
  rectangle "repack hybrid ISO\n(label preserved)" as Repack
}
M --> Seed
Blobs --> Pay
PLists --> Pay
Extract -> Seed -> Pay -> Menu -> Sq -> Repack

package "Emit target" {
  rectangle "dist/*.iso\nYUMI/Ventoy/iVentoy/dd" as ISO
  rectangle "write_usb\ndd | GRUB2 multiboot" as USB
  rectangle "netboot/  iPXE+HTTP | iVentoy" as Net
}
Repack --> ISO
Repack --> USB
Repack --> Net

rectangle "Target boot\nautoinstall + cloud-init" as Target
rectangle "disk-id guard\n(abort if mismatch)" as Guard
rectangle "fs layout btrfs|f2fs" as Fs
rectangle "adapters install()+apply_config()\nverify()" as Adapters

ISO --> Target
USB --> Target
Net --> Target
Target --> Guard
Guard --> Fs : match
Fs --> Adapters

note right of Adapters
  ollama adapter (reference):
  install clean from repo, then
  write override.conf, set OLLAMA_MODELS,
  restore shards as ollama:ollama,
  NEVER copy stale binaries.
end note

note right of Blobs
  Phase-2 seam: content-addressed
  blobs => P2P sync/ can replicate
  by hash range.
end note

@enduml
